title: Plan a request only when a wrong start would cost more than the plan; one owner writes it, signs anyone can count set who reads it, and Jeff decides only what is to be built and what cannot be undone.
pid: 6b88547d-78a8-4a64-a7e7-b754b201d97a
body: |2-
  What to do with a request for a change to skg, from the moment it
  arrives. Written for whoever coordinates (Top), on 2026-11-13, for
  Top's mission [[id:d59804d1-222c-4d26-b736-a0debde4e688][Write how a request that deserves a plan should be planned, checked and carried out by this team.]]
  The principle: a plan exists to make, in the open and once, the
  decisions that would otherwise be made silently, in code, by
  whichever mind gets there first. So plan when there are such
  decisions and they are dear to get wrong. Every step below is as
  cheap as it can be made, because missions run one at a time, Top's
  reading costs the most, and Jeff wants to be needed less.
  Each step ends with what it rests on. "Read" means a published
  source says it, in [[id:b034bd82-6ed1-48cb-81d5-d492db9209b3][what I read on planning, checking and carrying out work, and what I took from each]].
  "Ours" means I inferred it from how this team is shaped, often
  departing from a source, in [[id:7c1c9b52-05d2-4d67-8891-b1f937b06b39][where the planning procedure departs from its sources, because of how this team is shaped]].
  "?" marks a step I am unsure of; the trial that would tell is in
  [[id:0b103101-28e3-4380-8d26-e95a34f18dd5][what I am unsure of in the planning procedure, and the smallest trial that would tell]].
